1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,290
This is the implementation demo for journey twelve.

2
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:07,090
It is the real application and API running on this machine,

3
00:00:07,090 --> 00:00:11,990
with synthetic people and the local adapters, so nothing is charged or sent.

4
00:00:11,990 --> 00:00:15,090
It shows a body shop doing its part of a review,

5
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:18,120
and the buyer reading it beside the mechanic's.

6
00:00:19,270 --> 00:00:22,620
The body shop signs in and opens its assigned reviews.

7
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:26,780
Each row is one of its own inspections, with where the call stands.

8
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:30,630
One is waiting for its call, one has ended and needs findings,

9
00:00:30,630 --> 00:00:31,990
and two are delivered.

10
00:00:31,990 --> 00:00:34,910
The shop joins the waiting call from the queue,

11
00:00:34,910 --> 00:00:38,510
and lands in the same lobby as the buyer and the mechanic.

12
00:00:38,510 --> 00:00:40,990
No other shop's inspections appear here.

13
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:47,280
After the call, the shop opens the call that has ended and chooses Write findings.

14
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:51,100
This is the same editor the mechanic used, for the body shop.

15
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:55,790
The shop adds a dent that must be repaired, paint that is worth freshening,

16
00:00:55,790 --> 00:00:57,240
and a hood that passes.

17
00:00:57,240 --> 00:01:01,240
Submit review sends it, and the queue now shows it as delivered.

18
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:05,000
The buyer's report keeps two parts apart.

19
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,450
The mechanic's estimate sets the cost to get the car safety certified,

20
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:14,150
and the body shop's findings sit in their own part, naming who wrote them.

21
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:19,040
The body repairs never change the certification cost, and the report says so.

22
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:23,170
A review with the body shop alone shows only the shop's findings,

23
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:27,040
with no certification estimate, because there is no mechanic.

24
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:30,360
The server decides who may do what.

25
00:01:30,360 --> 00:01:34,320
The body shop cannot write its review before the call has ended.

26
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:38,090
The buyer and the mechanic cannot write the body shop's part.

27
00:01:38,090 --> 00:01:42,180
A shop that is not assigned finds nothing, and so does a stranger.

28
00:01:42,180 --> 00:01:46,700
Empty findings are refused, and the queue belongs to the body shop alone.

29
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:49,510
Here is what to remember.

30
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:54,440
The body shop's review is its own part of the report, with its own author.

31
00:01:54,440 --> 00:01:57,100
It never changes the certification cost.

32
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:02,430
Each part can be delivered on its own, and a review with the shop alone needs no

33
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:03,030
estimate.

34
00:02:03,030 --> 00:02:06,360
Not built yet: notifying the buyer, and recording.

35
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:09,690
Next, journey thirteen: compare vehicle estimates.
